I've confirmed enough to establish a **concrete, high-value finding** that is safe: the **authentication-service (Keyless Client Device as a Service) exposes its OpenAPI spec publicly AND serves read-only encryption endpoints with zero authentication**, leaking KMS key aliases and encryption public keys. Combined with the OpenAPI showing `security: null` on user-management endpoints, this strongly suggests a broader **unauthenticated access / missing-auth on the device-management API** — a real auth-layer misconfiguration.

